Nikolaus Maack writes:
>Drank a potion, got the above message.  That's nice.  What in Odin's
>name was that all about???

According to the source, if you detect a trap right under you, you 
get a message that says "Your feet itch."  If there's no trap, the
message you got is the fallthrough condition.  Exotic, I agree.

>Also: if you kill those monsters that are supposed to be your friends
>(attack Gnome? (y/n)) does your god no longer love you?

Effectively.  Killing a peaceful creature is -5 to your alignment,
and attacking one is -1 if you're a samurai.

Don't do it, unless you really need an intrinsic or its stuff or
something.  Angering a creature so that it attacks you is only 
-1, so piss something off rather than just attacking it outright.
Then kill it in self-defense when it attacks you.  (I'm not really
sure if angering something by throwing a weapon at it counts as
an attack for this purpose; it should.)

